cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Birding with AI: bird detection from an IP camera with BirdNET-Go, MQTT and Home Assistant"
message: "If you use this runbook, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  A self-hosted runbook and configuration snippets for detecting birds by sound
  with a security camera you already own. BirdNET-Go analyses the camera's RTSP
  audio, publishes detections to Home Assistant over MQTT, and Saezuri renders
  them as an illustrated collage. Covers stream verification, Docker Compose,
  a Caddy reverse proxy, Home Assistant template sensors, an automation and a
  dashboard, detection tuning, operations and troubleshooting. Detection runs
  locally: the audio never leaves the machine and no cloud account is required.
authors:
  - family-names: Rebbert
    given-names: Markus
repository-code: "https://github.com/mrebbert/Birding-with-AI"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-20"
keywords:
